    {
      "message": "When should I use WorkManager for persistent work on Android? Answer briefly with source citations.",
      "http_status": 200,
      "wall_seconds": 23.167,
      "request_id": "301fc0b9-5836-4afb-887a-3e996ce2f995",
      "session_id": "9367275f-db25-4112-b1a6-173034c303be",
      "answer": "Use **WorkManager** for work that must run reliably even if the user navigates away, the app exits, or the device restarts, such as sending logs/analytics to backend services or periodically syncing application data [S1]. Do not use it for in-process background work that can safely be terminated if the app process goes away [S1].\n\nFor comparison:\n*   Use **Coroutines** for all asynchronous work that doesn't need to persist if the app leaves the visible state, as they stop when the app closes [S2].\n*   Use **AlarmManager** only for precise alarms or notifications (e.g., calendar events), not for recurring background work, because it is less efficient regarding power and resource management [S2].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "citation_id": "S1",
          "chunk_id": "9eba32e6a6d8e331dd077239a27d35a00d4f9d9bec90c8741dcee482ad4b3b93",
          "title": "Task scheduling Stay organized with collections Save and categorize content based on your preferences.",
          "source": "workmanager.md",
          "source_url": "https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/background-tasks/persistent",
          "score": 0.8903182148933411,
          "line_start": 122,
          "line_end": 135,
          "page_start": null,
          "page_end": null,
          "quote": "## Use WorkManager for reliable work\n\nWorkManager is intended for work that is required to **run reliably** even if\nthe user navigates off a screen, the app exits, or the device restarts. For\nexample:\n\n* Sending logs or analytics to backend services.\n* Periodically syncing application data with a server.\n\nWorkManager is not intended for in-process background work that can safely be\nterminated if the app process goes away. It is also not a general solution for\nall work that requires immediate execution. Please review the [background\nprocessing guide](/guide/background) to see which solution meets your needs.\n\n",
          "truncated": false
        },
        {
          "citation_id": "S2",
          "chunk_id": "bdbba451bfb5a6eb5dcc7e9aa3a69f1651cbc2c492511faa14d4e6cbcb08601d",
          "title": "Task scheduling Stay organized with collections Save and categorize content based on your preferences.",
          "source": "workmanager.md",
          "source_url": "https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/background-tasks/persistent",
          "score": 0.8897165060043335,
          "line_start": 136,
          "line_end": 145,
          "page_start": null,
          "page_end": null,
          "quote": "## Relationship to other APIs\n\nThis table shows how WorkManager relates to similar APIs. This information can\nhelp you choose the right API for your app's requirements.\n\n| API | Recommended for | Relationship to WorkManager |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Coroutines** | All asynchronous work that doesn't need to persist if the app leaves the visible state. | Coroutines are the standard means of leaving the main thread in Kotlin. However, they stop as soon as the app closes. For work that should persist even after the app closes, use WorkManager. |\n| **AlarmManager** | Alarms only. | Unlike WorkManager's regular workers, AlarmManager's exact alarms wake a device from Doze mode. It is therefore not efficient in terms of power and resource management. Only use it for precise alarms or notifications such as calendar events, not for recurring background work. |\n\n",
          "truncated": false
        },
        {
          "citation_id": "S3",
          "chunk_id": "3298de9b338d9d877181de9569809da0583810c31591f2745b82e3979ed3a082",
          "title": "Task scheduling Stay organized with collections Save and categorize content based on your preferences.",
          "source": "workmanager.md",
          "source_url": "https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/background-tasks/persistent",
          "score": 0.8888211250305176,
          "line_start": 173,
          "line_end": 176,
          "page_start": null,
          "page_end": null,
          "quote": "#### Blogs\n\n* [Introducing WorkManager](https://medium.com/androiddevelopers/introducing-workmanager-2083bcfc4712)\n\n",
          "truncated": false
        }
